-- Vascular system & blood pressure regulation (medium-hard)
('Mean arterial pressure (MAP) is best approximated by which formula?', 'Diastolic BP + 1/3 (Pulse pressure)', 'Systolic BP + Diastolic BP / 2', 'Systolic BP - Diastolic BP', 'Diastolic BP x Heart rate', 'Diastolic BP + 1/3 (Pulse pressure)', 'Because diastole occupies ~2/3 of the cardiac cycle, MAP approximates DBP + 1/3(PP), or equivalently (SBP + 2xDBP)/3.', 1250, 'Physiology'),
