('In the proximal convoluted tubule, which substance is reabsorbed with Na+ via co-transport and is normally completely absent from final urine?', 'Glucose', 'Urea', 'Creatinine', 'Phosphate', 'Glucose', 'SGLT2 reabsorbs essentially all filtered glucose with Na+ in the proximal tubule; glucosuria occurs only when plasma glucose exceeds the renal threshold (~180 mg/dL).', 1000, 'Physiology'),
